mkn.gpu

CUDA/HIP C++20 convenience wrappers

======

Whether you are using CUDA or ROCM, we attempt to deduce from available headers.
If automatic detection fails, specify appropriate define like `-DMKN_GPU_CUDA=1`
Without CUDA or ROCM headers the CPU backend is used.
See: inc/mkn/gpu/def.hpp

Compile argument switches

Key             MKN_GPU_CUDA
Type            bool
Default         1 if cuda_runtime.h is found, else 0
Description     activate CUDA as impl of mkn::gpu::*

Key             MKN_GPU_ROCM
Type            bool
Default         1 if hip/hip_runtime.h is found, else 0
Description     activate ROCM as impl of mkn::gpu::*

Key             MKN_GPU_CPU
Type            bool
Default         1 if neither CUDA nor ROCM is active, else 0
Description     activate the CPU backend as impl of mkn::gpu::*, even when GPU headers are available

Key             MKN_GPU_FN_PER_NS
Type            bool
Default         0
Description     expose functions explicitly via
                   mkn::gpu::hip::*
                   mkn::gpu::cuda::*

Key             MKN_GPU_WARP_SIZE
Type            uint
Default         use manufacturer provided (eg warpSize), usually 32
Description     override use if defined

Key             MKN_GPU_TRACE
Type            bool
Default         1 for CUDA when NVTX3 headers are available, else 0
Description     profiler annotations (NVTX / roctx), see inc/mkn/gpu/trace.hpp
                   ROCM requires linking rocprofiler-sdk-roctx

Key             MKN_CPU_DO_NOT_DEFINE_DIM3
Type            bool
Default         false
Description     if true, skips defining dim3 struct which is usually provided by gpu headers
